id: pm-6qiwan
title: "One shared tracker-initialization guard: 48 sites re-implement resolvePmRoot plus a settings probe plus the same literal refusal, so every precision fix has to be applied 48 times and never is"
description: "Promote tracker-initialization detection into one public SDK guard and migrate the 48 hand-rolled CLI call sites to it. The shared primitive must distinguish missing roots, file collisions, and missing settings with precise recovery and a static replication gate."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[5]: "area:sdk",defect-recurrence,error-taxonomy,refactor,simplification
created_at: "2026-08-10T05:54:06.969Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-20T06:23:44.469Z"
closed_at: "2026-08-20T06:21:13.120Z"
completed_at: "2026-08-20T06:21:13.120Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 360
acceptance_criteria: "A single SDK guard owns the tracker-initialization refusal and all 48 call sites delegate to it; The guard distinguishes root-missing, root-is-a-file, and settings-missing, and each carries its own recovery; The recovery for root-is-a-file does not suggest pm init, which cannot succeed against a regular file; The surface-replication gate declares this set so a 49th hand-rolled copy fails CI"
parent: pm-usfg
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Replaced 50 replicated SDK initialization probes with one public shared preflight and added typed executable recovery plus a source adoption ratchet.
expected_result: "One SDK guard distinguishes missing root, non-directory root, and missing settings; file roots never recommend initialization; CI prevents new inline copies."
actual_result: All 50 invocations across 45 SDK modules delegate the shared guard; the 21-probe executable corpus passes all three filesystem states; the source ratchet reports zero forbidden copies.
component: "sdk/* command entrypoints, core/store/item-store"
